// @run
// @log 1
// @log v
// A NULLABLE UNION VARIANT HAS A REP, and this file is where it used to have none.
//
// `E | null` over a plain declared struct is the `nulstruct` NICHE: `(ref null $E)`, whose
// `fbValtype` slot is a row in the STANDALONE struct table. Make `E` a union arm anywhere in
// the module (the `y` line below) and `collectS` stops interning that row — the arm's values
// belong to the variant table — so the niche had no slot to name and the program was
// `emitProgram: ref valtype with no interned shape`.
//
// WHAT KEPT IT REFUSED AFTER THE `nulvariant` VKIND LANDED. `annCommitVariantMembers` did not
// register a declared struct the module also uses as a nullable inner: calling `E` a variant
// satisfied its union positions and broke this one, because the niche indexed the standalone
// struct table. That exclusion was written when there was no `nulvariant` VKind — this file's
// own text said "when it lands, drop the exclusion with it" — and the kind has since been
// built (`fbValtype`'s `nulvariant` arm, `retNulVariantFlag` / `nulVariantIndexOf` as the
// kind/slot PAIR). Dropped with it (silent-class-inventory D1031).
//
// THE SPELLING IS NOT AN INGREDIENT AND THAT IS WHY THE `y` LINE IS INLINE. The DECLARED
// spelling of the same union (`type U = string | E` + `const y: U = "v"`) has always run; only
// the inline one reached the exclusion, since the declaration route registers its members
// unconditionally. One program, two answers, decided by which spelling was written — the
// asymmetry this file now pins closed.
//
// `E | null` on its own — with no other union in the module — lowered and ran throughout, and
// a three-arm `string | E | null` is an ordinary box whose `null` rides a tag, not a niche.
type E = { code: i32, msg: string }
function a(): E | null { return { code: 1, msg: "m" } }
const r = a()
if r != null { print(r.code) } else { print(-1) }
const y: string | E = "v"
if y is E { print(y.code) } else { print(y) }
